cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Machine Learning-Based Multiphase CT Radiomics for Differentiating
  Hepatocellular Carcinoma from Hepatocellular Adenoma in Dogs: analysis code
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software (this record) and the
  associated journal article listed under "preferred-citation".
type: software
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23582592
date-released: "2026-10-22"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Seungheon354/dogct-hca-hcc"
keywords:
  - radiomics
  - machine learning
  - triple-phase CT
  - hepatocellular carcinoma
  - hepatocellular adenoma
  - veterinary imaging
  - SHAP
  - dog
abstract: >-
  Custom analysis pipeline for differentiating canine hepatocellular carcinoma
  (HCC) from hepatocellular adenoma (HCA) using radiomic features extracted from
  triple-phase contrast-enhanced CT. Includes multiphase feature preprocessing,
  SHAP-based feature ranking aggregated across stratified cross-validation folds,
  a sequential Top-N feature-selection and multi-model comparison framework
  (logistic regression, random forest, LightGBM, XGBoost, CatBoost, and
  histogram-based gradient boosting), together with the out-of-fold probability
  export used to construct the reported ROC curves.

